{"uid":"35a6f528067da6b9","name":"test_edit_then_check_and_uncheck_second_finding_preserves_body_in_browser","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_parked#test_edit_then_check_and_uncheck_second_finding_preserves_body_in_browser","historyId":"c164f6f7cbcb815f55dd50f13f6c0b5e","time":{"start":1791934352938,"stop":1791934362232,"duration":9294},"description":"cure-01-01-6 (B.3-B.4, D.1, DoD 2): the companion bug -- separator\n    insertion was tracked only at the instant the composed region grew\n    from zero active lines to one, so a hand edit typed directly into the\n    textarea BETWEEN two checks (leaving it unterminated again with one\n    waive line already active) never got its own leading separator\n    recorded. Checking F1, typing an unterminated further explanation,\n    then checking and unchecking F2 must leave the edited prose exactly\n    as typed, with F2's own composed line and its own separator fully\n    removed -- pinned through real keystrokes and real checkbox clicks.","descriptionHtml":"<p>cure-01-01-6 (B.3-B.4, D.1, DoD 2): the companion bug -- separator<br />\ninsertion was tracked only at the instant the composed region grew<br />\nfrom zero active lines to one, so a hand edit typed directly into the<br />\ntextarea BETWEEN two checks (leaving it unterminated again with one<br />\nwaive line already active) never got its own leading separator<br />\nrecorded. Checking F1, typing an unterminated further explanation,<br />\nthen checking and unchecking F2 must leave the edited prose exactly<br />\nas typed, with F2's own composed line and its own separator fully<br />\nremoved -- pinned through real keystrokes and real checkbox clicks.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791933345170,"stop":1791933345170,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldD